      "text": "Given four positive integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) such that:\n\\[\na \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nb \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nc \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nd \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when the sum of these integers \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11. Let's first express the sum in terms of the given congruences:\n\\[\na + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the given remainders:\n\\[\n2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11:\n\\[\n20 \\div 11 = 1 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 20 - 11 \\times 1 = 20 - 11 = 9\n\\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
