    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's denote the four positive integers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). According to the problem, when these integers are divided by 11, the remainders are 2, 4, 6, and 8, respectively. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\nWe are asked to find the remainder when the sum of these four integers \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11. First, we express the sum \\(a + b + c + d\\) in terms of the remainders:\n\\[ a + b + c + d = 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the remainders:\n\\[ 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11. We perform the division:\n\\[ 20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9 \\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[ 20 = 11 \\cdot 1 + 9 \\]\nThus, the remainder when 20 is divided by 11 is 9. Therefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]",
